  # Missile Weapons Specifications
  Notes:
  - Munition range and ammo capacity is taken from the standard magazine and ammunition that comes loaded with the weapon.
  - For munitions that accelerate over time (such as missiles), range is a rough estimate.
  - For munitions that are fired at a static speed (such as normal weapons), range is simply just the launch velocity * projectile lifetime.
  - RPS may not be accurate due to it being capped by server tick speed (usually 20 or 30 ticks/second).
  - Most, albeit not all, missile weapons use physical ammunition and must be loaded by hand or autoloader system. They do not have have an infinite fallback.
  - Most, albeit not all, missile weapons have a homing system, tracking to a grid's piloting console or drone core. The level of tracking depends on the warhead. You can't lock on, so mind your friends!

